Relay Hub itself has no server component: GitHub Pages serves static files
and the proxy runs in the visitor's browser. If you run a modified Relay
Hub as a network service (for example by adding a backend), the AGPL
requires you to offer your users the corresponding source.

Third-party network services, not distributed with this software:

  Public Wisp endpoints — operated by third parties; Relay Hub probes a
  pool of them and uses the fastest that answers from your network, or a
  custom endpoint you configure in Settings.

  Public CORS mirrors (allorigins, codetabs, corsproxy.io, cors.lol,
  cors.workers.dev) — used only by Simple mode, only when Scramjet cannot
  reach a Wisp endpoint.
